-/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-   GRAPHICS — the shape language.
-
-   Three primitives, used everywhere: a filled brand chip that carries an icon,
-   a flat geometric diamond, and a soft tint wash. Nothing here is a gradient
-   glow or a drop shadow pretending to be paper — flat blocks with real spacing
-   is what makes a page read as confident rather than decorated.
-   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
-
-/* The chip: a solid brand circle carrying a white icon. This is the single most
-   recognisable graphic element — it turns a plain list into a designed one. */
-/* The badge was a solid --accent disc with a line glyph on it. Six saturated
-   discs is a lot of brand on one page, and — worse — the glyph inside was from
-   a THIRD icon set, so the six things the home page promises were drawn one way
-   here and a different way once you were inside the product.
-   It is the same tile the in-app page heads use, holding the same mark. */
-.featureIconWrap {
-  width: 54px;
-  height: 54px;
-  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
-  background: var(--surface);
-  border: 1px solid var(--blush-line);
-  display: grid;
-  place-items: center;
-  margin-bottom: 18px;
-  box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(var(--text-rgb), .06);
-  transition: transform var(--transition-slow) var(--ease-out),
-              box-shadow var(--transition-slow) var(--ease-out);
-}
-/* The mark brings its own colours — see SectionMark.module.css. */
-.featureIcon {
-  display: block;
-}
-
-.featureCard:hover .featureIconWrap {
-  transform: translateY(-3px) rotate(-6deg);
-  box-shadow: 0 10px 26px rgba(var(--text-rgb), .12);
-}
-
-/* Every other chip alternates to the deeper fill, so a grid of six reads as a
-   composition rather than six identical dots. */
-/* White → blush → ink, the same three grounds the page rotates through. The
-   mark's tone is switched in the JSX to match, since an ink hairline on the
-   ink badge would be invisible. */
-.featureCard:nth-child(3n+2) .featureIconWrap {
-  background: var(--blush);
-  border-color: var(--blush-deep);
-  box-shadow: none;
-}
-
-.featureCard:nth-child(3n) .featureIconWrap {
-  background: var(--text);
-  border-color: var(--text);
-  box-shadow: none;
-}
-
-/* The diamond — a 45°-rotated square, the reference's core decorative form.
-   Purely presentational, so it is aria-hidden at the call site. */
-.gfxDiamond {
-  position: absolute;
-  border-radius: 22%;
-  transform: rotate(45deg);
-  pointer-events: none;
-}
-
-/* A soft tint wash behind a section, to break the run of white without
-   introducing another colour. */
-.gfxWash {
-  position: absolute;
-  border-radius: 50%;
-  filter: blur(60px);
-  opacity: .5;
-  pointer-events: none;
-}
-
-/* ── Product showcase — the real app, not an illustration of it ──────────── */
-.showcase {
